From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:51:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] [User Education] Restructure ShowPromoInPage for memory
 safety

This CL does two things:
 - Ensures that help bubble factories are set up in all browser
   configurations, even if other user education services are not. It is
   possible to show a help bubble as a simple UI annotation even in
   browsers (such as incognito) where IPH is not available - for example
   via ShowPromoInPage.
 - Restructures ShowPromoInPageImpl so that:
   * Constructor never self-deletes.
   * Code paths and callbacks are easier to follow.
   * Guards are put around callbacks to detect self-deletion.
   * More failure conditions are explicitly detected.

This combination of changes should completely avoid the issues in the
attached bug, however unlikely they may be (at some point, CHECKs would
have also prevented these issues, but also crashed the browser).

